A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate only when the **supported cause matches** an open ticket
([decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause), replacing decision 0001):

1. Read the report; resolve its tenant, locale, form version and channel.
2. Compare the failure mechanism and evidence with the target ticket.
3. Merge only for the same supported cause. Keep distinct or uncertain cases separate.
4. Count unique report IDs, preserving source evidence and correcting classifications
   when new information arrives. Keep triaging incoming reports during an incident.

<Callout>
Subjects and browser-locale intake tags are hints, not proof. Identical subjects can
describe different causes, and different subjects can describe the same cause.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Do not merge. Request missing tenant details or reproduction evidence. Keep anomalous
reports visible and distinguish a tentative classification from a verified root cause.
An existing “known” status does not establish that a new report is a duplicate.

